00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.030 align:start position:0%
EU agricultural ministers have given  their backing for a coordination  facility to be set up to help develop  additional tools to control diseases in  niche crops such as fruit vegetables and  flowers the use of plant protection  products like herbicides on minor crops  is too small to be sustainable for  industry even though growers need them  and this leads to a shortage of such  products in the sector for this  coordinating facility will be funded by  a co-financing procedure by the  Commission to the tune of three hundred  and fifty thousand euros a year for the  next three years measured by another  250,000 euros each year by the Member  States and this will help to launch  projects but to coordinate experiences  and best practices and also form as you  said Minister a database on the issue  according to the European Commission the  direct impact of losses due to pests or  diseases from niche crops in the EU  totals more than 1 billion euros each  year the ministers also discussed food  waste in Europe and considered a  suggestion to exempt more products with  long shelf lives from the requirement to  have best before dates on their  packaging
 

